  <diagram id="page26" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2000" dy="1400" grid="0" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="2400" background="#FFFFFF">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="b0" value="&lt;b&gt;QUESTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;S7.1: Is branch manager history required to be non-overlapping, and are acting regional directors recorded as managers?&lt;br&gt;S7.1: Are employee email, national ID, customer email, tax ID, and phone globally unique?&lt;br&gt;S7.3: How should overlapping category-rate periods be prevented, and can rates have open-ended ValidTo?&lt;br&gt;S7.5: Can a GPS device be uninstalled or reassigned, requiring installation history?&lt;br&gt;S7.7: Can a person be both an Egyptian national-ID holder and passport holder; which identifier is required?&lt;br&gt;S7.7: Can a customer have multiple blacklist entries or be reinstated?&lt;br&gt;S7.7 and Section 8: How should a corporate authorized driver who is also an individual customer be matched across the two records?&lt;br&gt;S7.10: Are points earned per rental fixed, and what are the exact tier balance rules after redemption?&lt;br&gt;S7.12: Can corporate main driver be omitted for a corporate rental; should walk-in be distinguished from absent reservation?&lt;br&gt;S7.12: How are extension dates/vehicles/agents constrained against the preceding agreement?&lt;br&gt;S7.16: How are refunds/chargebacks represented, and may one payment cover multiple rentals?&lt;br&gt;S7.16: Are corporate invoices grouped by calendar month and how are invoice adjustments represented?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="30" width="1700" height="404" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b1" value="&lt;b&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;S7.1: EmployeeID is the employee supertype PK; agent/mechanic subtype membership is exclusive; DB age/hire checks use date-based logic.&lt;br&gt;S7.1: Manager history is the temporal source of truth; current manager is the open-ended row. Branch telephone values are multivalued.&lt;br&gt;S7.3: Category rate periods for the same category may not overlap; rates are positive and the latest applicable date is used.&lt;br&gt;S7.5: Each device can be installed in at most one vehicle at a time; installation record represents current assignment only.&lt;br&gt;S7.7: Individual is identified by exactly one of NationalID or PassportNo; customer subtype is total and disjoint.&lt;br&gt;S7.1, S7.3, and S7.7: UQ constraints on employee national ID/email, customer identifiers, tax number, SIM, and catalog names are design assumptions where uniqueness is not explicit.&lt;br&gt;S7.1: HireDate must be at least 21 years after DOB; commission is constrained to 0-15% and salary/monetary rates are non-negative or positive as appropriate.&lt;br&gt;S7.7: A company driver is identified by (CorporateCustomerNo, DriverNo); its driver row is deleted with the corporate account. Personal customer records are not automatically merged with driver records.&lt;br&gt;S7.10: Loyalty balance and tier are derived from ledger sum; points value is signed, with transaction type specifying earned/redeemed.&lt;br&gt;S7.11-12: Reservation number and rental number are separate keys; a reservation yields zero or one rental; each reservation conversion preserves customer/category.&lt;br&gt;S7.12: Corporate authorized driver is referenced by company plus DriverNo; additional drivers are stored as rental-specific snapshots.&lt;br&gt;S7.15: Damage repair link uses composite (RentalNo, ReportNo); at most one maintenance job per damage report.&lt;br&gt;S7.16: TransactionReference is optional for cash and required for card/bank; payments are rental-scoped.&lt;br&gt;S7.16: Monthly corporate invoice is modeled as one invoice linked to one or more rentals for a corporate customer.&lt;br&gt;S7.7 and Section 8: A corporate driver who is also an individual customer remains two linked only if manually resolved; no shared person identity is stated." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="446" width="1700" height="497" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b2" value="&lt;b&gt;CONTRADICTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct wording contradictions found. S7.3 category pricing says daily price is by category, while the COO note gives some luxury vehicles a separate price; modeled as a vehicle-specific rate override is an open question/assumption.&lt;br&gt;S7.1 says every employee is assigned to one branch, while S7.1 says regional director temporarily replaces a resigning manager; assumed regional director is assigned to a branch and has a manager-history record.&lt;br&gt;S7.16 describes payment per rental, while Finance note says corporate clients receive one monthly invoice; modeled corporate invoices aggregating rentals, but invoice settlement/payment ownership needs confirmation." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="955" width="1700" height="125" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page27" name="4-Business-Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2000" dy="1400" grid="0" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="2400" background="#FFFFFF">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="b0" value="&lt;b&gt;RULE 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SRS section: 7.6 and Interview Notes (Section 8)&lt;br&gt;Rule: Vehicle transfers must move between different branches, from the vehicle’s current physical branch; movement must preserve chronological location history and its odometer cannot move backward.&lt;br&gt;Why constraints are not enough: This compares a new transfer to the prior transfer and current vehicle location, requiring cross-row chronological lookup.&lt;br&gt;Enforcement: Stored procedure creates transfer in a transaction, locks the vehicle, checks FromBranch != ToBranch and equals current location, validates odometer &amp;gt;= latest recorded, inserts transfer, updates current branch. Deny direct updates." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="30" width="1700" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b1" value="&lt;b&gt;RULE 2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SRS section: 7.12 and Interview Notes (Section 8)&lt;br&gt;Rule: A corporate rental main driver must be an authorized driver belonging to that rental’s corporate customer; individual rentals are driven by the individual customer.&lt;br&gt;Why constraints are not enough: The rule depends on customer subtype and matching corporate account across Rental and AuthorizedDriver.&lt;br&gt;Enforcement: Rental creation procedure validates subtype, authorization membership, and driver; enforce with transactional application logic or trigger." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="198" width="1700" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b2" value="&lt;b&gt;RULE 3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SRS section: 7.3 and Interview Notes (Section 8)&lt;br&gt;Rule: Vehicle status changes must record the employee and exact change time; status transitions must remain consistent with open rentals and maintenance jobs.&lt;br&gt;Why constraints are not enough: Requires a history insert and checks against related active records, not a row-local constraint.&lt;br&gt;Enforcement: Trigger on status update appends old/new status, timestamp, employee from session context, and rejects invalid transitions after checking active rentals/jobs." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="366" width="1700" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b3" value="&lt;b&gt;RULE 4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SRS section: 7.10 and Interview Notes (Section 8)&lt;br&gt;Rule: Loyalty tier is determined by the customer’s current ledger balance and must never be manually entered.&lt;br&gt;Why constraints are not enough: Tier depends on SUM across multiple ledger rows and changes after each entry.&lt;br&gt;Enforcement: Compute as a view/query or persisted computed process recalculated transactionally on ledger insert; disallow manual tier edits." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="534" width="1700" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b4" value="&lt;b&gt;RULE 5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SRS section: 7.1&lt;br&gt;Rule: Every branch must always have exactly one current manager, and an employee must not manage overlapping branches at the same time.&lt;br&gt;Why constraints are not enough: It requires checking overlapping effective date ranges and uninterrupted coverage across multiple history rows.&lt;br&gt;Enforcement: Use a manager-assignment procedure with serializable transactions and temporal overlap checks; reject closing the active row until a replacement manager is assigned." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F8FA;strokeColor=#47647C;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="702" width="1700" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>